<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=movable-type">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Writing and counting</p><h1 class="enc-title">Movable type</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Movable type is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> system using individual, reusable characters that can be arranged to form texts. It was invented in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bi-sheng">Bi Sheng</a> in the eleventh century under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>, using ceramic type. Printing flourished under the Song, though woodblock printing remained dominant in China.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/movable-type.jpg" alt="Movable type" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willi Heidelbach · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metal_movable_type.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Bi Sheng invented <b>movable type</b> using ceramic characters around 1040, some four centuries before Gutenberg's printing press.</blockquote><a href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>The Auspicious Tantra of All-Reaching Union, a 449-page Tangut text found in the ruins of the Baisigou Square Pagoda in the Helan Mountains, is the earliest surviving book printed with wooden <b>movable type</b>; twelve Tangut titles printed with movable type survive today.</blockquote><a href="/empire/western-xia">Western Xia · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>The Bible was the earliest major book printed in Europe with mass-produced metal <b>movable type</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-24">24 August in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 1040</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>China</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/encyclopedia/bi-sheng">Bi Sheng</a> · <a href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Whether Asian movable type influenced Gutenberg is debated.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/woodblock-printing">Woodblock printing<span>before 220 CE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">Printing press<span>c. 1440</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=movable-type">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
